F FurthestOver                 | OcclusionCulling.slang  | 38-61   | -                         | -  | The furthest ordinate recorded across the region one partition covers. so that a two-by-two reading spans the whole extent, which is what makes the test one constant-cost comparison per partition rather than a walk proportional to what it covers. and the four texels are read at the origin; reading at nought instead compares every partition against the depth recorded in the display's first corner, which admits nothing and rejects everything.
    in    Tested  TestedPartition  [-]  the classified partition, its origin and span in display texels
    out   -       Depth            [-]  the least ordinate of the four texels read; reversed, so the furthest point
    note  📐 Four texels and no more, whatever the partition's projected extent. `SelectLevel` chooses the level
    note  🔴 The **origin** is read as well as the span, and both are needed. The level is chosen from the span

