//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

F Compact                      | OcclusionCulling.slang  | 74-91   | -                         | -  | Appends one partition's triangle run to the surviving ordinals and advances the record's corner count. and dividing the prior value by three gives the run's own base — a second counter for the base would be a second ordering the two atomics have no guarantee of agreeing on. run leaves the fan's triangle ordinals interleaved with another partition's, and the draw then issues one partition's corners against another's positions.
    in    Tested  TestedPartition  [-]  ?
    out   -       void             [-]  ?
    note  🔴 One atomic and not two. The corner count is three times the triangle count, so advancing the count
    note  ⚠️ A run that would overrun the surviving span is dropped whole rather than written short. A partial

