F DepthOccludes                | OcclusionUniform.slang  | 126-129 | -                         | -  | Whether one partition stands wholly behind what the reduction recorded. The conservative reduction is therefore the **minimum**, and a partition is occluded when its nearest ordinate is at or below the furthest ordinate recorded across the region it covers. artist meets it as an object flickering along its own edge rather than as a comparison inverted.
    in    NearestDepth  float     [-]  the partition's nearest ordinate; reversed, so the greatest of its eight corners
    in    ReducedDepth  float     [-]  the least ordinate the covered region carries; the furthest point recorded there
    out   -             Occluded  [-]  true only where nothing of the partition can reach in front of what stands
    by    Shader/OcclusionCulling.slang
