F ProjectObjectPosition        | VisibilityUniform.slang | 149-174 | nonallocating,nonthrowing | ✔️ | Projects one object-space position through the composed transform. applied with an implicit unit fourth ordinate rather than with a stored one — the position is a point and never a direction, so the alternative is a component that is unity at every call site. bits by the host and narrowed once. One product per corner and no second transform: a shader applying a placement and then a projection has narrowed the intermediate, and that intermediate is the document position whose width `02` rebases precisely to avoid spending. negating a depth after the projection has reversed it has reversed it twice, and the image is the inside of every object rather than an image that sorts wrongly.
